+# Fix: Railway Frontend Build Error (EBUSY)
+
+## Problem
+```
+npm error EBUSY: resource busy or locked, rmdir '/app/node_modules/.vite'
+```
+
+This happens because Vite's cache directory is locked during the build process on Railway.
+
+## Solution 1: Skip Cleanup (Try This First)
+
+**Build Command:**
+```bash
+npm ci && npm run build
+```
+
+Just use the standard build command without trying to remove `.vite`. Railway's fresh builds shouldn't have this issue.
+
+## Solution 2: Use npm install Instead
+
+If Solution 1 doesn't work, try:
+
+**Build Command:**
+```bash
+npm install && npm run build
+```
+
+`npm install` is more forgiving than `npm ci` and might handle the locked directory better.
+
+## Solution 3: Build Without Clean Install
+
+**Build Command:**
+```bash
+npm install --prefer-offline && npm run build
+```
+
+This uses cached packages and might avoid the lock issue.
+
+## Solution 4: Force Clean Build (Nuclear Option)
+
+If nothing else works:
+
+**Build Command:**
+```bash
+npm install --force && npm run build
+```
+
+## Recommended: Start with Solution 1
+
+1. Go to Railway frontend service → Settings → Build & Deploy
+2. Set Build Command to: `npm ci && npm run build`
+3. Redeploy
+
+If that fails, try Solution 2, then 3, then 4.
+
+## Why This Happens
+
+Railway's Docker build environment sometimes locks files during the build process. The `.vite` cache directory can get locked, preventing cleanup. Using a simpler build command often works better.
